reference yield for kharif 2025-26: Gujarat kharif, kg/ha, DA&FW Directorate of Economics and Statistics,
five-year table at 3rd Advance Estimates. The four prior seasons are shown so the reader can place 2025-26.
  crop           2021-22   2022-23   2023-24   2024-25   2025-26   rank/5   vs prior mean   Y_ref used
  Rice             2304      2496      2449      2362      1675       1          69.7 %        1675  paddy
  Maize            1950      1906      2013      1474      2035       5         110.9 %        2035  grain
  Bajra            2442      1775      1776      1844      1362       1          69.5 %        1362  grain
  Groundnut        2262      2579      2757      2665      2734       4         106.6 %        2734  unshelled pods
  Cotton            559       602       574       513       551       2          98.0 %        1621  seed cotton (kapas)
  Cotton is published as lint and converted to seed cotton at a 34% ginning outturn.
  Rice and bajra recorded their LOWEST yield of the five years and maize its highest. Gujarat kharif 2025 was an
  excess-rain season, not simply a wet one: the state announced flood relief for Vadodara district after the Narmada
  overflowed 16-18 September 2025, inside the grain-fill window for paddy. The rainfall anomaly above corroborates
  the direction; it is deliberately NOT used as a multiplier, because the official estimate already measures the outcome.
  No Vadodara district uplift is applied, because no district-level 2025-26 estimate is published. Vadodara ranks
  1st in Gujarat for maize yield and 2nd for cotton, so those two forecasts are conservative by a known sign.

