reserved-scene integrity: no module outside s2_ndvi/validate/figures names ndvi_R1 or ndvi_R2

1. RESERVED OPTICAL -- 2025-12-12 and 2026-01-16, read by nothing upstream. n=813
   Both dates are post-kharif and inside the rabi window, so they cannot score the yield forecast.
   They test two specific pre-registered claims.

   1a. cotton must be the greenest label on 12 December
       crop        n   NDVI 12 Dec   NDVI 16 Jan   NDVI 10 Jun
       Bajra      112         0.474         0.647         0.356
       Cotton      58         0.690         0.742         0.232
       Groundnut  257         0.532         0.541         0.403
       Maize      277         0.505         0.565         0.378
       Rice       109         0.502         0.601         0.591
       highest: Cotton  -> PASS
       one-sided Mann-Whitney cotton > rest on 12 Dec: p=1.26e-11

   1b. perennial parcels must be green in December AND in June
       10 Jun  perennial 0.247   rest 0.397   FAIL   p(greater)=1.0e+00 p(less)=1.1e-04
       12 Dec  perennial 0.777   rest 0.519   PASS   p(greater)=1.6e-05 p(less)=1.0e+00
       16 Jan  perennial 0.756   rest 0.568   PASS   p(greater)=4.9e-04 p(less)=1.0e+00
       -> FALSIFIED on June. June radar level -20.24 vs -20.42 dB (p=0.71): bare like everything else.
       -> 9 of 12 never fall more than 0.5 dB between consecutive passes, and all stay green to 16 Jan.
       -> Not an orchard. A long-duration crop sown with the monsoon and still standing in January
          (sugarcane and banana both fit, and both are grown in Vadodara). The screen's actual
          claim -- not one of the five kharif annuals -- survives.

   1c. NEGATIVE control -- plots cleared of kharif by 12 Nov should be under rabi in December,
       not bare. If they were bare, the reserved scene would be measuring kharif and 1a would mean
       something different from what it claims.
       cleared (>0.8) n= 196  NDVI 12 Dec 0.488   standing (<0.2) n= 160  0.613
       population median 12 Dec 0.520 -- cleared plots are NOT bare (control holds)

2. LOOK-DIRECTION CONTROL -- is the T5 anomaly geometry rather than crop state?
   elongated parcels only (axis ratio >= 1.5), n=650
   rho(angle to the T5 look, t5_anomaly)       = -0.051 (p=0.195)
   rho(cos 2*(row azimuth - look), t5_anomaly) = +0.051 (p=0.195)
   threshold |rho| = 0.2; verdict: clean
   T5's LEVEL is not used anywhere regardless: `farm_features` replaces it with the T4-T6
   interpolation, and only the residual `t5_anomaly` survives as a weak covariate.

3. SPATIAL COHERENCE -- Moran's I, 8 nearest neighbours
   yield forecast         I=+0.279  (permutation mean -0.001, p<0.001, 0/999 permutations reached it)
   season integral        I=+0.187  (permutation mean -0.001, p<0.001, 0/999 permutations reached it)
   within-crop residual   I=+0.151  (permutation mean -0.001, p<0.001, 0/999 permutations reached it)
   Null is 999 permutations, so the smallest p this test can report is 1/1000 = 0.001.
   Neighbouring fields share soil, water and management, so positive I on the forecast is expected.
   Positive I on the residual means real spatial structure the crop label alone does not carry;
   I near zero would mean the residual is plot-level noise.

